mmit e465ea285c4): _cli_tracker applies the existing shared pins (tests/_git_upkeep.apply_upkeep_pins: gc/maintenance autoDetach=false), the same fix class bare remotes already use. New guard test traces the fixture under a forced-detach GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL with GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1: an unpinned control records a --detach maintenance child, the pinned fixture records upkeep but none detached. Mutation check: removing the pin call turns the guard RED (assert [['git','mai...','--detach']] == []), restoring it GREEN. Stress: the module plus the flaky test, 200 rounds under -n 4, 200/200 passed (19:24-19:36 PST). No config key, env var, flag or helper added. make verify running outside the sandbox.","timestamp":1794454714783833487},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion evidence 2026-11-11 21:43 PST (session 3d705fec): `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` on e465ea285c4579e5b0c5d40413be1f37cca2b657 (19:55-21:00 PST): exit 0 — default tier 21093 passed / 29 skipped, integration 218 passed / 2 skipped. Log .rebar/worktrees/fix-fulmar/.rebar/scratch/3d705fec/make-verify-fulmar2.log. (An earlier run at 19:38 was killed externally at 50% with exit 144 and no failures recorded; the orphaned-load check found nothing left over.) Gerrit 3360 submitted via gerrit_safe_submit.py at that revision with LLM-Review +1 / Verified +1 / 0 unresolved; merged as 6dbf05538f776495c31ccb37b6241ba95a2e8bb1 (server-side rebase, test file identical). make lint inside verify ran the mechanism ratchet (exit 0): no new mechanism, env var, config key or helper.","timestamp":1794462173820921186},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-11 21:49 PST (session 3d705fec): CLOSED as preexisting through the completion gate (21:43-21:49 PST). Fix landed via Gerrit 3360, merged 6dbf05538f776495c31ccb37b6241ba95a2e8bb1. The status check before close reported stale-code, because the plan's one dependency file is the file this fix changed; the close gate accepted the close.","timestamp":1794462563089591565}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794387176978229273,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"df733a73-4b8a-4aee-a50a-babd4de5fa31","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ed07-b103-3e7b-4c50"},{"link_uuid":"386926c3-1b35-488a-852f-71cf88e751ad","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b8f7-65be-ec00-4844"},{"link_uuid":"271bcb7d-4902-4d78-8234-316e2ad620e8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6d05-ffa4-8da3-4479"},{"link_uuid":"b9d139f2-18d0-4499-a445-949ac40a7590","provenance":"derived","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"4e3e-d36f-53b9-4c1e"}],"description":"## Observation\n\n`tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck_keyset_prev.py::test_store_snapshot_survives_git_maintenance_but_still_catches_mutation` failed once under a full `make verify` (2026-11-11 00:20-00:50 PST, commit 4d21c744977). Line 254 `lock.unlink()` raised `FileNotFoundError` for `<tmp>/churn/.tickets-tracker/.git/objects/maintenance.lock`; the test had written that file two lines earlier. Run alone it passed 6/6.\n\n## Root cause (measured)\n\n- The fixture `_cli_tracker` builds the tracker with a raw `git commit`. A GIT_TRACE2_EVENT trace of that commit on this host (git 2.56.0) records one child: `git maintenance run --auto --quiet --detach`.\n- git's `maintenance_run_tasks` (builtin/gc.c) takes `<objects>/maintenance.lock` before any task's auto condition is checked, then `daemonize()`s while still holding it, and the background child releases it with `rollback_lock_file`, which unlinks the path. With `--auto`, a lock it cannot take is skipped silently.\n- So `git commit` returns while a daemon still owns `objects/maintenance.lock`. If the test writes the lock inside that window, the daemon's rollback deletes the test's file and the test's own `unlink` fails. Load (4 xdist workers) widens the window, which is why it shows only under `make verify`.\n- Change 3351 (334295da063) does not interact: it suppresses auto maintenance only in `run_git_bounded`/`run_git_reaped`; the flaky test never invokes the CLI (bridge fsck's own git calls are plain `run_git` reads and a `rev-parse`, none of which run auto maintenance). The daemon comes from the fixture's raw `git commit`.\n- The class: a non-bare fixture repository built with raw git whose commit leaves detached upkeep running while the test reads or writes `.git`. `tests/_git_upkeep.py` already fixes the same class for bare remotes (`BARE_REMOTE_UPKEEP_PINS`: `gc.autoDetach=false`, `maintenance.autoDetach=false`); with those pins git runs auto maintenance in the foreground, so the lock is released before the command returns.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. In `_cli_tracker`, call the existing `apply_upkeep_pins(tracker / \".git\")` (from `tests/_git_upkeep.py`, the single definition of the pins) right after `git init`, before the fixture commit. No new helper, test setting, env var or config key.\n2. Add `test_cli_tracker_leaves_no_detached_upkeep` to the same module. With `monkeypatch.setenv` it sets `GIT_TRACE2_EVENT` to a per-test trace file, `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL` to a tmp gitconfig forcing `maintenance.auto=true`, `maintenance.autoDetach=true`, `gc.autoDetach=true`, and `GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1`, so host config cannot mask either result. Positive control, built inline (no shared builder): `git init` plus `git commit --allow-empty` without the pins records a `git maintenance run` child with `--detach` (existing `maintenance_children` reader). Then, with a fresh trace, `_cli_tracker` records no such child with `--detach`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck_keyset_prev.py`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The fixture's commit records no detached `git maintenance run` child under GIT_TRACE2_EVENT, and an unpinned control repository records one; pinned by the new test.\n- [x] The flaky test and the rest of the module pass 200 consecutive runs under `pytest -n 4`.\n- [x] No new config key, env var, flag or test helper is added.\n- [x] [non-codebase] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review.\n  provenance: environment=macOS dev host, fix-fulmar worktree; principal=Rebar Bot Nava; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=live-call — exit status and log live outside the repository\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck_keyset_prev.py","reason":"pin fixture upkeep; guard test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","6d05-ffa4-8da3-4479"],["relates_to","b8f7-65be-ec00-4844"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a46d20c4-5a3b-45ca-a1ce-b16b35eb9ff6","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"422a-8867-4b6d-4900","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Recurrence: bridge fsck maintenance-lock test still races git maintenance under make verify","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["88af9d2d-1d7a-4dd0-a3fb-9fe61df3de2f","866bd98c-4e45-4867-9548-854f9842e08c","67a8dddc-798a-47af-ae36-0b22689b6e96","6baf5043-6317-47be-bcee-e8db71f14fe8","77786608-e1e7-4481-bab7-d43aa0f30f21","da64e0fa-dd86-4433-aedd-a1ad032a9395","a0e57a5e-f201-4446-83af-69267d03f59d","99af710b-f556-4a67-9fd5-0cb6150286b9","9cef016b-5862-401c-a545-6178a9e3d2d0","271bcb7d-4902-4d78-8234-316e2ad620e8","a46d20c4-5a3b-45ca-a1ce-b16b35eb9ff6","e7e12542-29aa-40af-bcc3-d4217f9601b8","b9d139f2-18d0-4499-a445-949ac40a7590","91da800d-20b8-4f1c-bf20-45394005983f"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794462563089591566,"uuid":"a25f68eb-1a25-4158-b582-46d5c5aa256b"}